ady O from previous move.\n\nWait, in this scenario:\n\nAfter X plays A1, O plays C3.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 X | B1 . | C1 O\n\nA2 . | B2 X | C2 .\n\nA3 O | B3 . | C3 O\n\nX plays B1.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 X | B1 X | C1 O\n\nA2 . | B2 X | C2 .\n\nA3 O | B3 . | C3 O\n\nO\'s turn. O can play B3, which completes row 3 (A3 O, B3 O, C3 O). So O wins.\n\nOh no! So if X plays A1 and then B1, O wins.\n\nThat\'s bad. So playing A1 might be dangerous.\n\nSimilarly, if X plays C3 first.\n\nX plays C3.\n\nO plays A1.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 O | B1 . | C1 O\n\nA2 . | B2 X | C2 .\n\nA3 O | B3 . | C3 X\n\nNow, O has column A (A1, A3) and needs A2.\n\nX must block A2.\n\nX plays A2.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 O | B1 . | C1 O\n\nA2 X | B2 X | C2 .\n\nA3 O | B3 . | C3 X\n\nNow, X has row 2 (A2, B2), threatens C2.\n\nO plays C2 to block.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 O | B1 . | C1 O\n\nA2 X | B2 X | C2 O\n\nA3 O | B3 . | C3 X\n\nX\'s turn. Valid moves: B1, B3.\n\nX plays B1.\n\nO plays B3.\n\nDraw.\n\nSo in this line, it\'s a draw.\n\nBut in the previous line where X played A1 and then B1, O won. So playing A1 can be risky if X doesn\'t block properly.\n\nSo maybe A1 is not the best move.\n\nLet\'s consider another option: B1.\n\nX plays B1.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 . | B1 X | C1 O\n\nA2 . | B2 X | C2 .\n\nA3 O | B3 . | C3 .\n\nO\'s best move is to block column B by taking B3.\n\nO plays B3.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 . | B1 X | C1 O\n\nA2 . | B2 X | C2 .\n\nA3 O | B3 O | C3 .\n\nX\'s turn. Valid moves: A1, A2, C2, C3.\n\nX can play A2, threatening row 2.\n\nX plays A2.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 . | B1 X | C1 O\n\nA2 X | B2 X | C2 .\n\nA3 O | B3 O | C3 .\n\nO must block row 2 by taking C2.\n\nO plays C2.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 . | B1 X | C1 O\n\nA2 X | B2 X | C2 O\n\nA3 O | B3 O | C3 .\n\nX\'s turn. Valid moves: A1, C3.\n\nX plays A1.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 X | B1 X | C1 O\n\nA2 X | B2 X | C2 O\n\nA3 O | B3 O | C3 .\n\nNow, X has column A (A1, A2), but A3 is O. Row 1 has X, X, O. No win.\n\nX could play C3.\n\nBoard:\n\nA1 . | B1 X | C1 O\n\nA2 X | B2 X | C2 O\n\nA3 O | B3